\end{itemize}

\section{Discussion}
The unified DMDE-USE framework demonstrates that dark matter and dark
energy can be co-evolved within a single, coherent simulation organism
without sacrificing numerical stability. This architecture enables:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Exploration of non-standard dark energy models.
    \item Study of filament and halo formation under varying expansion
    histories.
    \item Integration with quantum cosmology modules (e.g., Wheeler-DeWitt
    boundary conditions) within UW-SIE v2.0.
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}
UW-SIE v2.0, via the DMDE-USE engine, provides a robust platform for
